The extrinsic camera parameters will model the 3D rotation, which is mainly around the $X$-axis (we will ignore the translation of the origin):
$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{R}
= 
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & 0 & 0\\
0 & \cos(\theta) & -\sin(\theta) \\ 
0 & \sin(\theta) & \cos(\theta) 
\end{bmatrix}.
\end{aligned}
$$

